t back."}, {"turn": 13, "text": "H5 was the 12k's worst move, at 7.2 points lost. The engine wanted D4, and instead the lead went from +0.7 to -6.5. This was the turning point of the game."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "D6 lost another 4.0 points and took Black's lead from -6.5 to -10.5. After this Black never got back within 9 points."}, {"turn": 18, "text": "Opus 5.5's D4 matched the engine's first choice and lost just 0.3 points, with Black's lead at -12.1. White's strong row across the third and fourth lines was shaping up, and from here Opus 5.5 played precisely."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties with a danger flag, and count.py only flood-fills empty regions to tally territory plus komi on a given position. Both work on the current position, and neither chooses, scores or ranks candidate moves or looks ahead.", "stop": false}}